OL,3,GNEWSALook North sofa to be pushed 80
OL,4,Amiles for Children in Need
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe wife of rugby league legend Rob
OL,7,FBurrow will join BBC Look North
OL,8,Fpresenter Amy Garcia for this year's
OL,9,FChildren in Need charity challenge.
OL,11,FLindsey Burrow and Amy plan to push the
OL,12,Fprogramme's red sofa 80 miles (129km)
OL,13,Facross Yorkshire over five days,
OL,14,Fcovering 12-20 miles each day.
OL,16,FThe pair will start at Ripon on Monday
OL,17,F9 November and pass through South
OL,18,FYorkshire before crossing the finish
OL,19,Fline in Wakefield on Friday 13
OL,20,FNovember. Their efforts will be
OL,21,Fbroadcast live along the route.
OL,23,APub: 14-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
